  "narrative": {
    "intro": "W W Grainger reported $295M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 17.6% year over year. W W Grainger recorded 146,995 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $2K. Fiscal-year obligations rose from $198M in FY21 to $358M in FY25, then moved to $295M in FY26. The General Services Administration accounted for the vast majority of FY2026 to date obligations, with $292M. Home Centers is the largest NAICS market for W W Grainger in FY2026 to date, with $293M. Other notable agency and market totals for FY2026 to date include the Department of Transportation with $909K and All Other Miscellaneous Electrical Equipment and Component Manufacturing with $396K. This summary focuses on contract obligations and award counts through the fiscal year to date and excludes full-year totals for the current fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has W W Grainger's federal business trended year over year?",
        "body": "W W Grainger's obligations fell 17.6% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations moved from $198M in FY21, to $210M in FY22, $264M in FY23, $320M in FY24, $358M in FY25, and $295M in FY26. The company recorded 146,995 awards in FY2026 to date, with an average award size of $2K. These figures reflect contract obligations through the fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers and what markets drive W W Grainger's federal receipts?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration is the largest buyer for FY2026 to date, with $292M in obligations. Home Centers is the top NAICS market for FY2026 to date, with $293M. Other agencies with FY2026 to date obligations include the Department of Transportation with $909K and the Department of Justice with $427K. Additional NAICS markets for FY2026 to date include All Other Miscellaneous Electrical Equipment and Component Manufacturing with $396K and Motor and Generator Manufacturing with $282K."
      }
    ]
  },
